        "market_heading": "Why home staging matters in the Montreal market",
        "market_text": "<p>Montreal's housing stock is unlike anywhere else in Canada: duplexes and triplexes with tenant-occupied units, century-old walk-ups with unusual room shapes, and a fast-growing stock of new condos. Empty or cluttered, these spaces are hard for buyers to read — home staging shows what the crooked-charming rooms of a Plateau flat actually hold.</p><p>Many plex listings are photographed mid-tenancy. Our free furniture removal digitally clears the tenant's belongings first, then stages the space clean — no awkward photos, no waiting for a vacancy.</p><p>The plex market is the reason this matters so much here. A triplex buyer is underwriting three units they will mostly never see empty, and photos taken around a tenant's furniture make that impossible to assess. Cleared and staged, each unit can be judged on its own layout and light.</p>",
